# Panes of the core on ROS 2 for 'RUN-TMUX-SESSION.bash', in the standard windows 'tools', 'user', and 'host' of every session of a platform on ROS 2, after the standard windows 'robot' and 'extra' of the platform, the extensions, and the setup.
# Each line reads '<layouts> <window> <launch-file> [<arg:=value> ...]', where '<layouts>' is '*' or a comma-separated list such as 'default-gazebo,default-realworld'.
# The word 'shell' opens a shell inside the Docker container, and the word 'host' opens a shell on the Ubuntu development machine.
# The FlexBE WebUI takes the place of the FlexBE App of ROS 1, as the first pane of the window 'tools'.

*  tools  openrosde_launch:flexbe_webui_default.launch.xml
*  tools  openrosde_launch:rqt_suite_default.launch.xml
*  tools  openrosde_launch:rosbridge_server_default.launch.xml
*  user   openrosde_user_launch:user_example_default.launch.xml
*  user   shell
*  host   host
